 subject here.","D":"They does not agree with is and does not serve as preparatory it."}}},{"id":"93812f6d-e9fc-57fd-ab1b-a6228fb3d984","topicSlug":"noun-clauses","level":"B2","prompt":"Complete the content clause: “We know that she ____ the survey results every week.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"compares"},{"id":"B","text":"compare"},{"id":"C","text":"to compare"},{"id":"D","text":"been compared"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"A **that-clause** has its own subject and finite verb.","explanation":"The that-clause is finite, so **she compares** uses present agreement.","keywords":["finite-that-clause"],"skill":"finite-that-clause","contextKey":"noun-clauses-48","fingerprint":"affd56a6a97f335680e3b43ca79ca9a840801e7dbf406c549066048a25ccbc1f","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-questions-reference"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A **that-clause** has its own subject and finite verb.","The that-clause is finite, so **she compares** uses present agreement.","Choose **compares**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The that-clause is finite, so **she compares** uses present agreement.","B":"The third-person singular subject requires -s in this affirmative clause.","C":"A to-infinitive is not a finite verb after she.","D":"Been would need an auxiliary and does not fit this active present-simple clause."}}},{"id":"b86722d8-aa42-5836-aa5c-2e738a046e54","topicSlug":"noun-clauses","level":"B2","prompt":"Choose the polite indirect question about the evening meal.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Could you tell me why she prepares the evening meal?"},{"id":"B","text":"Could you tell me why does she prepare the evening meal?"},{"id":"C","text":"Could you tell me why she prepare the evening meal?"},{"id":"D","text":"Could you tell me why she to prepare the evening meal?"}],"answerId":"A","h